# -*- mode: sh; sh-shell: bash -*-
# vim: set ft=bash:
# shellcheck shell=bash
# shellcheck disable=SC2016

### Retrieval over the Hermes log corpus -- what the logs of this host say about <X>, in one call
###
### Hermes writes a corpus of text on this host: the agent and gateway logs, one worker transcript
### per kanban task, one output document per cron run, and the session store.  The corpus is large
### (megabytes, millions of lines) and reading it with ad hoc pipelines -- 'grep' here, 'sed' there,
### a 'sqlite3' query next -- costs several turns and floods an agent's context with raw
### transcripts.  'hermes_logs' is the one deterministic answer instead: it streams the corpus once,
### prints a bounded digest of the matching lines and keeps the complete match list on disk.
###
###   please hermes_logs --grep <ere> --since 1d      # a bounded digest and the exact total
###   please hermes_logs --grep <ere> --count         # only the number
###   please hermes_logs --grep <ere> --json | jq .   # one object for a wrapper
###
### THE CORPUS (explicit, never guessed)
###
### One *corpus root* is a Hermes home directory; the default is '$HERMES_HOME' and falls back to
### '~/.hermes'.  A root contributes the sources below, and only these -- nothing is searched
### implicitly, no directory is discovered by walking:
###
###   logs       <root>/logs/*.log, *.log.gz             the agent/gateway/gui logs
###   workers    <root>/kanban/logs/*.log, *.log.gz      one worker transcript per kanban task
###   cron       any file below <root>/cron/output/      'cron/output/<job>/<stamp>.md' and the
###                                                       flat legacy 'cron/output/<job>_*.txt'
###   sessions   <root>/sessions/*.jsonl, *.jsonl.gz     diverted (transcript) session records
###   store      <root>/state.db                         the SQLite session store, read only
###
### The root is overridable with '--root <dir>' (repeatable) or with the environment variable
### BAR_HERMES_LOGS_ROOT (':' separated); '--root' wins.  Other Hermes profiles are addressed with
### '--root ~/.hermes/profiles/<name>', never by guessing: a path that differs between the gateway,
### the TUI and a worker is exactly what an agent must not hardcode.  With more than one root every
### locator carries the index of its root ('#2/logs/agent.log:88') and one 'corpus:' line names each.
###
### THE ANSWER (one record per matching line)
###
###   <locator> <TAB> <timestamp> <TAB> <snippet>
###
###   locator       '<source path>:<line>' relative to its root ('logs/agent.log:1234'), so
###                 'sed -n 1234p <root>/logs/agent.log' retrieves the line byte for byte.  A store
###                 record has no file line and reads 'state.db:<session>/<message>/<line>', which
###                 'sqlite3 -readonly <root>/state.db' resolves with 'where id=<message>'.
###   timestamp     'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS' local time -- the stamp on the line when it has one (at the
###                 line start for a log line, anywhere on a JSON record), otherwise the stamp of the
###                 newest line above it that had one, otherwise the file's modification time.  A
###                 leading '~' marks those two derived cases, an exact stamp carries no marker.  A
###                 store record carries the message's own timestamp.
###   snippet       the line with its control characters removed, clipped at
###                 BAR_HERMES_LOGS_SNIPPET characters (default 160) with the number of characters
###                 left out appended as '<+N>'.  Tabs separate the fields; a snippet never holds one.
###
### Then the totals, as lines of their own and never implied:
###
###   corpus: <root> [<sources scanned>]   matches: <n>   shown: <s> of <n> (limit <l> lines, <c> chars)
###   clipped: <k> snippet(s) at <c> chars   unreadable: <u> source(s) not scanned: <name>..
###   max: <path>
###
### 'matches' is the exact number of matching lines, a hard assertion: it is the count the scan
### produced over exactly the sources the 'corpus:' lines name, and it is qualified by 'unreadable'
### when a source could not be read.  The digest prints at most '--limit' match lines (default 20,
### BAR_HERMES_LOGS_LIMIT) and at most BAR_HERMES_LOGS_BYTES characters of them (default 1200), so
### the answer stays around a kilobyte however busy the corpus is.  Whenever anything stays unshown
### the complete match list is on disk before anything is printed and its absolute path is printed as
### 'max:'.  That file holds every match ('<locator> <TAB> <timestamp> <TAB> the whole line'), up to
### BAR_HERMES_LOGS_MAX records (default 20000) -- beyond that the file is capped and 'max:' says so.
### It is written below BAR_HERMES_LOGS_DIR (default $TMPDIR) and named after the query, so the same
### question reuses one file and the answer stays retrievable.
###
### FILTERS
###
###   --grep <ere>     an extended regular expression, matched against every line of every scanned
###                    source with 'grep -E' semantics.  Without it every line matches (the digest is
###                    still bounded, the count still exact).  It is the only thing that decides what
###                    counts: no keyword prefilter, no sampling, no ranking.
###   --since <when>   '<n>[smhdw]' (ago) or anything GNU 'date -d' accepts ('2026-10-10',
###                    '2026-10-10 08:00:00'); records before the cutoff are dropped.  In the store
###                    the range is pushed into SQL, which makes a bounded session query cheap.
###   --source <kind>  restrict to a source kind, repeatable.
###   --task <sel>     keep only the sources whose path contains <sel>: '--task t_deadbeef' keeps a
###                    worker transcript, '--run 2026-10-10' the cron run of that day.  Applied to
###                    the source path, so the store never matches a task selector.
###   --session <id>   keep only the records of that session: store rows whose session id contains it
###                    (in SQL), 'sessions/<id>.jsonl' files by name, and the lines of every other
###                    source by their text (the agent logs carry '[<session-id>]').
###   --count          the number alone -- it wins over '--json', because one number is already the
###                    machine form.  Nothing is elided here, so no 'max:' line is printed.
###
### EXIT CODES: 0 answered, matches found.  3 answered, no match ('grep' semantics: an answer, not a
### failure -- the count is printed).  2 usage error.  1 could not answer: a root is not a directory,
### or a source could not be read -- the digest is still printed, marked with 'unreadable:' and with
### the reason on stderr, and the count then covers only what was readable.
###
### NON GOALS: no summarisation, no judgement, no LLM, no ranking -- it is a filter.  It does not
### replace the 'session_search' tool for fuzzy recall, and it does not read what Hermes stores
### outside the paths above (the kanban board as a database, cron job definitions, the vault).  It
### never pages, never colours, and prints no progress on stdout.

# helper-module: hermes

require json_lib

declare -gx BAR_HERMES_LOGS_ROOT="${BAR_HERMES_LOGS_ROOT:-}"            ## ':' separated corpus roots, '--root' wins
declare -gx BAR_HERMES_LOGS_LIMIT="${BAR_HERMES_LOGS_LIMIT:-20}"        ## match lines the digest prints
declare -gx BAR_HERMES_LOGS_SNIPPET="${BAR_HERMES_LOGS_SNIPPET:-160}"   ## characters kept of a matching line
declare -gx BAR_HERMES_LOGS_MAX="${BAR_HERMES_LOGS_MAX:-20000}"         ## records kept in the full match list
declare -gx BAR_HERMES_LOGS_BYTES="${BAR_HERMES_LOGS_BYTES:-1200}"      ## characters of match records the digest prints
declare -gx BAR_HERMES_LOGS_DIR="${BAR_HERMES_LOGS_DIR:-}"              ## where the full match list is written

# The query context of a running call ('Q_') and its result ('R_', plus the run state 'HERMES_LOGS_*'
# below).  One call runs in one shell; the rule body is the only writer of 'Q_', 'hermes_logs_scan'
# the only writer of 'R_'.
declare -g  HERMES_LOGS_Q_PAT="" HERMES_LOGS_Q_ICASE="" HERMES_LOGS_Q_CUTOFF="" HERMES_LOGS_Q_EPOCH=""
declare -g  HERMES_LOGS_Q_TASK="" HERMES_LOGS_Q_SESSION="" HERMES_LOGS_Q_LIMIT=0 HERMES_LOGS_Q_SNIP=0
declare -g  HERMES_LOGS_Q_MAX=0 HERMES_LOGS_Q_COUNT="" HERMES_LOGS_Q_JSON="" HERMES_LOGS_Q_TAG=""
declare -g  HERMES_LOGS_Q_BYTES=0
declare -ga HERMES_LOGS_Q_KINDS=() HERMES_LOGS_Q_ROOTS=()
declare -g  HERMES_LOGS_R_TOTAL=0 HERMES_LOGS_R_CLIPPED=0 HERMES_LOGS_R_KEPT=0 HERMES_LOGS_R_SHOWN=0
declare -g  HERMES_LOGS_R_BYTES=0 HERMES_LOGS_R_UNREADABLE=0
declare -g  HERMES_LOGS_R_HITS="" HERMES_LOGS_R_CLIP="" HERMES_LOGS_R_STAT=""
declare -ga HERMES_LOGS_R_LOST=() HERMES_LOGS_ENV=()
declare -gA HERMES_LOGS_R_USED=()
declare -g  HERMES_LOGS_PROGRAM=""

function hermes_logs_usage
{
    cat >&2 <<'USAGE'
usage: bar hermes_logs [--grep <ere>] [-i] [--since <when>] [--source <kind>].. [--task <sel>]
                       [--session <id>] [--limit <n>] [--count] [--json] [--root <dir>]..

  --grep <ere>       keep only lines matching the extended regular expression
  -i, --ignore-case  match the pattern case insensitively
  --since <when>     keep records at or after <when>: '<n>[smhdw]' ago ('90m', '1d') or an
                     absolute time ('2026-10-10', '2026-10-10 08:00:00')
  --source <kind>    scan only this source kind, repeatable: logs workers cron sessions store
  --task <sel>       keep only sources whose path contains <sel> ('--task t_deadbeef')
  --session <id>     keep only the records of that session
  --limit <n>        at most <n> match lines in the digest
  --count            print the exact number of matching lines and nothing else
  --json             print one JSON object instead of lines
  --root <dir>       corpus root, repeatable; overrides BAR_HERMES_LOGS_ROOT;
                     default $HERMES_HOME or ~/.hermes
USAGE
    return 2
}

function hermes_logs_selector ## <option> <value> - reject a selector neither SQL nor the shell can carry
{
    if [[ "$2" == *[[:cntrl:]]* ]]; then
        printf 'hermes_logs: %s may not contain control characters\n' "$1" >&2
        return 1
    fi
    return 0
}

function hermes_logs_since ## <when> - resolve '--since' into HERMES_LOGS_Q_CUTOFF and Q_EPOCH
{
    ## The cutoff is the local 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS' the line timestamps are compared against (for
    ## that shape a lexicographic comparison is a chronological one), the epoch is the same instant
    ## for the SQL range.  Both are set here, or the call fails.
    local when="$1" n unit secs epoch
    case "$when" in
    *[0-9][smhdw])
        n="${when%?}"
        [[ "$n" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]] || return 1
        unit="${when: -1}"
        case "$unit" in
        s) secs=1 ;;
        m) secs=60 ;;
        h) secs=3600 ;;
        d) secs=86400 ;;
        w) secs=604800 ;;
        esac
        epoch="$(( $(date +%s) - n * secs ))"
        ;;
    *)
        epoch="$(date -d "$when" +%s 2>/dev/null)" || return 1
        [[ -n "$epoch" ]] || return 1
        ;;
    esac
    HERMES_LOGS_Q_CUTOFF="$(date -d "@$epoch" '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S')" || return 1
    HERMES_LOGS_Q_EPOCH="$epoch"
    return 0
}

function hermes_logs_wanted ## <kind> [kind..] - is this source kind wanted? (no kind: all)
{
    (( $# == 1 )) && return 0
    local kind
    for kind in "${@:2}"; do
        [[ "$kind" == "$1" ]] && return 0
    done
    return 1
}

function hermes_logs_emit_files ## <root> <index> <kind> [file..] - source records, sorted by path
{
    ## One record per file: '<kind>\t<index>\t<relpath>\t<mtime>', the mtime in the shape of a line
    ## timestamp, so a source without timestamps is still dated.
    local root="$1" index="$2" kind="$3"
    shift 3
    (( $# )) || return 0
    local file
    printf '%s\n' "$@" | LC_ALL=C sort -u | while IFS= read -r file; do
        printf '%s\t%s\t%s\t%s\n' "$kind" "$index" "${file#"$root"/}" \
            "$(date -r "$file" '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S')"
    done
}

function hermes_logs_files ## <root> <index> [kind..] - the corpus of one root as source records
{
    local root="$1" index="$2"
    shift 2
    local file
    local -a files=()
    if hermes_logs_wanted logs "$@"; then
        for file in "$root"/logs/*.log "$root"/logs/*.log.gz; do
            if [[ -f "$file" ]]; then files+=( "$file" ); fi
        done
        hermes_logs_emit_files "$root" "$index" logs ${files[@]+"${files[@]}"}
        files=()
    fi
    if hermes_logs_wanted workers "$@"; then
        for file in "$root"/kanban/logs/*.log "$root"/kanban/logs/*.log.gz; do
            if [[ -f "$file" ]]; then files+=( "$file" ); fi
        done
        hermes_logs_emit_files "$root" "$index" workers ${files[@]+"${files[@]}"}
        files=()
    fi
    if hermes_logs_wanted cron "$@"; then
        if [[ -d "$root/cron/output" ]]; then
            while IFS= read -r file; do files+=( "$file" ); done \
                < <(find "$root/cron/output" -type f 2>/dev/null)
        fi
        hermes_logs_emit_files "$root" "$index" cron ${files[@]+"${files[@]}"}
        files=()
    fi
    if hermes_logs_wanted sessions "$@"; then
        for file in "$root"/sessions/*.jsonl "$root"/sessions/*.jsonl.gz; do
            if [[ -f "$file" ]]; then files+=( "$file" ); fi
        done
        hermes_logs_emit_files "$root" "$index" sessions ${files[@]+"${files[@]}"}
        files=()
    fi
    if hermes_logs_wanted store "$@" && [[ -f "$root/state.db" ]]; then
        printf '%s\t%s\t%s\t%s\n' store "$index" state.db \
            "$(date -r "$root/state.db" '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S')"
    fi
    return 0
}

function hermes_logs_program ## - the awk filter, one program for a text source and for the store
{
    ## It reads its query from the environment ('HL_*') and not from 'awk -v': '-v' would interpret
    ## backslash escapes in the pattern and silently search for a different expression.  It streams:
    ## one line in, at most two records out (the full match list and the digest), never a buffer of
    ## matches.  A store row is '<session> 0x1f <message> 0x1f <timestamp> 0x1f <content>', the
    ## content's newlines encoded as 0x01.
    cat <<'AWK'
BEGIN {
    OFS = "\t"
    US = sprintf("%c", 31)
    NL = sprintf("%c", 1)
    mode = ENVIRON["HL_MODE"]
    pat = ENVIRON["HL_PAT"]
    ses = ENVIRON["HL_SES"]
    icase = ENVIRON["HL_ICASE"] + 0
    cutoff = ENVIRON["HL_CUTOFF"]
    loc = ENVIRON["HL_LOC"]
    mtime = ENVIRON["HL_MTIME"]
    snip = ENVIRON["HL_SNIP"] + 0
    limit = ENVIRON["HL_LIMIT"] + 0
    budget = ENVIRON["HL_BYTES"] + 0
    max = ENVIRON["HL_MAX"] + 0
    hits = ENVIRON["HL_HITS"]
    clip = ENVIRON["HL_CLIP"]
    if (icase)
        pat = tolower(pat)
    total = 0
    clipped = 0
    kept = 0
    shown = 0
    used = 0
    last = ""
}

function text(line,   s) {
    s = line
    gsub(/\t/, " ", s)
    gsub(/[[:cntrl:]]/, "", s)
    gsub(/  +/, " ", s)
    sub(/^ /, "", s)
    sub(/ $/, "", s)
    return s
}

function stamp(line,   t) {
    exact = 1
    if (match(line, /^[ \t]*[[]?[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9][ T][0-9][0-9]:[0-9][0-9]:[0-9][0-9]/)) {
        t = substr(line, RSTART, RLENGTH)
        sub(/^[ \t[]+/, "", t)
    } else if (substr(line, 1, 1) == "{" && match(line, /[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9][ T][0-9][0-9]:[0-9][0-9]:[0-9][0-9]/)) {
        t = substr(line, RSTART, RLENGTH)
    } else {
        exact = 0
        if (last != "")
            return last
        return mtime
    }
    gsub(/T/, " ", t)
    last = t
    return t
}

function emit(line, at, ts, isexact,   full, brief, n, record) {
    if (pat != "" && (icase ? tolower(line) : line) !~ pat)
        return
    if (cutoff != "" && ts < cutoff)
        return
    total++
    if (kept < max) {
        full = text(line)
        print at, (isexact ? ts : "~" ts), full >> hits
        kept++
    }
    if (shown < limit) {
        brief = text(line)
        n = length(brief) - snip
        if (n > 0) {
            clipped++
            brief = substr(brief, 1, snip) " <+" n ">"
        }
        record = at "\t" (isexact ? ts : "~" ts) "\t" brief
        if (used + length(record) + 1 <= budget) {
            print record >> clip
            used += length(record) + 1
            shown++
        }
    }
}

mode == "file" {
    if (ses != "" && index($0, ses) == 0)
        next
    t = stamp($0)
    e = exact
    emit($0, loc ":" FNR, t, e)
    next
}

mode == "store" {
    nf = split($0, f, US)
    if (nf < 4)
        next
    session = f[1]
    mid = f[2]
    ts = f[3]
    content = f[4]
    for (i = 5; i <= nf; i++)
        content = content US f[i]
    nf = split(content, part, NL)
    for (i = 1; i <= nf; i++)
        emit(part[i], "state.db:" session "/" mid "/" i, ts, 1)
    next
}

END {
    print total, clipped, kept, shown, used
}
AWK
}

function hermes_logs_scan_file ## <file> <locator> <mtime> <session-filter> - scan one text source
{
    local file="$1" loc="$2" mtime="$3" ses="$4" rc=0
    : >"$HERMES_LOGS_R_STAT"
    if [[ "$file" == *.gz ]]; then
        if ! command -v gzip >/dev/null; then
            printf 'hermes_logs: gzip is not installed, %s is not scanned\n' "$file" >&2
            return 1
        fi
        gzip -dc "$file" | env "${HERMES_LOGS_ENV[@]}" HL_MODE=file HL_LOC="$loc" HL_MTIME="$mtime" \
            HL_SES="$ses" awk "$HERMES_LOGS_PROGRAM" >"$HERMES_LOGS_R_STAT" || rc=$?
    else
        env "${HERMES_LOGS_ENV[@]}" HL_MODE=file HL_LOC="$loc" HL_MTIME="$mtime" HL_SES="$ses" \
            awk "$HERMES_LOGS_PROGRAM" "$file" >"$HERMES_LOGS_R_STAT" || rc=$?
    fi
    return "$rc"
}

function hermes_logs_scan_store ## <db> <locator> <mtime> - scan the session store, read only
{
    ## The store is read with 'sqlite3 -readonly': it never creates a journal and never touches the
    ## live writer's WAL.  '--since' is pushed into SQL and the session selector becomes
    ## 'instr(session_id, ..)' so that it stays a substring match and no LIKE wildcard changes its
    ## meaning.  The content is deliberately *not* prefetched by keyword: the pattern decides what
    ## counts, in awk, exactly as it does for a file.  A newline inside a message is encoded as 0x01
    ## and a stray 0x1f as 0x1e, so one row is one input line; both are control characters and are
    ## removed from the snippet anyway.
    local db="$1" loc="$2" mtime="$3" rc=0 selector
    : >"$HERMES_LOGS_R_STAT"
    if ! command -v sqlite3 >/dev/null; then
        printf 'hermes_logs: sqlite3 is not installed, %s is not scanned\n' "$db" >&2
        return 1
    fi
    local sql="select session_id, id, datetime(timestamp,'unixepoch','localtime'),"
    sql="$sql replace(replace(coalesce(content,''), char(10), char(1)), char(31), char(30))"
    sql="$sql from messages"
    if [[ -n "$HERMES_LOGS_Q_EPOCH" ]]; then
        sql="$sql where timestamp >= $HERMES_LOGS_Q_EPOCH"
    fi
    if [[ -n "$HERMES_LOGS_Q_SESSION" ]]; then
        selector="${HERMES_LOGS_Q_SESSION//\'/\'\'}"
        if [[ -n "$HERMES_LOGS_Q_EPOCH" ]]; then
            sql="$sql and"
        else
            sql="$sql where"
        fi
        sql="$sql instr(session_id, '$selector') > 0"
    fi
    sqlite3 -readonly -separator $'\037' "$db" "$sql" |
        env "${HERMES_LOGS_ENV[@]}" HL_MODE=store HL_LOC="$loc" HL_MTIME="$mtime" \
            awk "$HERMES_LOGS_PROGRAM" >"$HERMES_LOGS_R_STAT" || rc=$?
    return "$rc"
}

function hermes_logs_used ## <kind> <root-index> - remember which sources one root contributed
{
    local kinds="${HERMES_LOGS_R_USED[$2]:-}"
    if [[ " $kinds " != *" $1 "* ]]; then
        HERMES_LOGS_R_USED[$2]="${kinds:+$kinds }$1"
    fi
    return 0
}

function hermes_logs_report_text
{
    ## The digest: the bounded match lines, then the totals as lines of their own.
    local index
    local -i shown="$HERMES_LOGS_R_SHOWN"
    if [[ -s "$HERMES_LOGS_R_CLIP" ]]; then
        cat "$HERMES_LOGS_R_CLIP"
    fi
    for index in "${!HERMES_LOGS_Q_ROOTS[@]}"; do
        printf 'corpus: %s [%s]\n' "${HERMES_LOGS_Q_ROOTS[$index]}" "${HERMES_LOGS_R_USED[$index]:-nothing}"
    done
    printf 'matches: %s\n' "$HERMES_LOGS_R_TOTAL"
    if (( shown < HERMES_LOGS_R_TOTAL )); then
        printf 'shown: %s of %s (limit %s lines, %s chars)\n' "$shown" "$HERMES_LOGS_R_TOTAL" \
            "$HERMES_LOGS_Q_LIMIT" "$HERMES_LOGS_Q_BYTES"
    fi
    if (( HERMES_LOGS_R_CLIPPED )); then
        printf 'clipped: %s snippet(s) at %s chars\n' "$HERMES_LOGS_R_CLIPPED" "$HERMES_LOGS_Q_SNIP"
    fi
    if (( HERMES_LOGS_R_UNREADABLE )); then
        printf 'unreadable: %s source(s) not scanned: %s\n' "$HERMES_LOGS_R_UNREADABLE" \
            "${HERMES_LOGS_R_LOST[*]}"
    fi
    if (( shown < HERMES_LOGS_R_TOTAL || HERMES_LOGS_R_KEPT < HERMES_LOGS_R_TOTAL )); then
        if (( HERMES_LOGS_R_KEPT < HERMES_LOGS_R_TOTAL )); then
            printf 'max: %s (the first %s of %s matches)\n' "$HERMES_LOGS_R_HITS" \
                "$HERMES_LOGS_R_KEPT" "$HERMES_LOGS_R_TOTAL"
        else
            printf 'max: %s\n' "$HERMES_LOGS_R_HITS"
        fi
    fi
    return 0
}

function hermes_logs_report_json
{
    ## The same numbers and the same records as one object, for a wrapper.
    local locator stamp text exact kind index canon
    local -a roots=() sources=() hits=()
    local -A seen=()
    while IFS=$'\t' read -r locator stamp text; do
        exact="true"
        if [[ "$stamp" == "~"* ]]; then
            exact="false"
            stamp="${stamp#\~}"
        fi
        hits+=( "$(printf '{"locator":%s,"timestamp":%s,"exact":%s,"text":%s}' \
            "$(json_string "$locator")" "$(json_string "$stamp")" \
            "$exact" "$(json_string "$text")")" )
    done <"$HERMES_LOGS_R_CLIP"
    for index in "${!HERMES_LOGS_Q_ROOTS[@]}"; do
        roots+=( "$(json_string "${HERMES_LOGS_Q_ROOTS[$index]}")" )
    done
    for index in "${!HERMES_LOGS_R_USED[@]}"; do
        for kind in ${HERMES_LOGS_R_USED[$index]}; do
            seen[$kind]=1
        done
    done
    for canon in logs workers cron sessions store; do
        if [[ -n "${seen[$canon]:-}" ]]; then
            sources+=( "$(json_string "$canon")" )
        fi
    done
    local since="null" ica="false"
    if [[ -n "$HERMES_LOGS_Q_CUTOFF" ]]; then
        since="$(json_string "$HERMES_LOGS_Q_CUTOFF")"
    fi
    if [[ -n "$HERMES_LOGS_Q_ICASE" ]]; then
        ica="true"
    fi
    printf '{"bar_hermes_logs":1,"pattern":%s,"ignore_case":%s,"since":%s,"roots":%s,"sources":%s,' \
        "$(json_string "$HERMES_LOGS_Q_PAT")" "$ica" "$since" \
        "$(json_array ${roots[@]+"${roots[@]}"})" \
        "$(json_array ${sources[@]+"${sources[@]}"})"
    printf '"matches":%s,"shown":%s,"kept":%s,"limit":%s,"max_records":%s,"bytes_budget":%s,"clipped":%s,"unreadable":%s,"max":%s,' \
        "$HERMES_LOGS_R_TOTAL" "$HERMES_LOGS_R_SHOWN" "$HERMES_LOGS_R_KEPT" "$HERMES_LOGS_Q_LIMIT" \
        "$HERMES_LOGS_Q_MAX" "$HERMES_LOGS_Q_BYTES" "$HERMES_LOGS_R_CLIPPED" "$HERMES_LOGS_R_UNREADABLE" \
        "$(json_string "$HERMES_LOGS_R_HITS")"
    printf '"hits":%s}\n' "$(json_array ${hits[@]+"${hits[@]}"})"
    return 0
}

function hermes_logs_scan ## - scan the corpus of HERMES_LOGS_Q_ROOTS and print the answer
{
    ## Streams every source once, appends every match to the full match list (bounded by
    ## HERMES_LOGS_Q_MAX), keeps the digest records (bounded by HERMES_LOGS_Q_LIMIT) and prints one
    ## of the three answers.  Returns the exit code of the module's contract.
    local kind idx rel mtime root locator ses
    local -i index rc=0 matches=0 snippets=0 records=0 drawn=0 drawnbytes=0 kept_budget=0 show_budget=0
    local -i byte_budget=0
    local dir="${BAR_HERMES_LOGS_DIR:-${TMPDIR:-/tmp}}"

    if [[ ! -d "$dir" ]]; then
        mkdir -p "$dir" || return 1
    fi
    HERMES_LOGS_R_HITS="$dir/hermes_logs-$HERMES_LOGS_Q_TAG.matches"
    HERMES_LOGS_R_CLIP="$dir/hermes_logs-$HERMES_LOGS_Q_TAG.digest"
    HERMES_LOGS_R_STAT="$dir/hermes_logs-$HERMES_LOGS_Q_TAG.stat"
    if ! : >"$HERMES_LOGS_R_HITS"; then
        printf 'hermes_logs: cannot write the full match list to %s\n' "$HERMES_LOGS_R_HITS" >&2
        return 1
    fi
    : >"$HERMES_LOGS_R_CLIP"

    HERMES_LOGS_PROGRAM="$(hermes_logs_program)"

    while IFS=$'\t' read -r kind idx rel mtime; do
        [[ -n "$kind" ]] || continue
        if [[ -n "$HERMES_LOGS_Q_TASK" && "$kind/$rel" != *"$HERMES_LOGS_Q_TASK"* ]]; then
            continue
        fi
        if [[ "$kind" == sessions && -n "$HERMES_LOGS_Q_SESSION" \
            && "$rel" != *"$HERMES_LOGS_Q_SESSION"* ]]; then
            continue
        fi
        root="${HERMES_LOGS_Q_ROOTS[idx]}"
        locator="$rel"
        if (( ${#HERMES_LOGS_Q_ROOTS[@]} > 1 )); then
            locator="#$(( idx + 1 ))/$rel"
        fi
        ses=""
        case "$kind" in
        sessions|store) ;;
        *) ses="$HERMES_LOGS_Q_SESSION" ;;
        esac
        hermes_logs_used "$kind" "$idx"
        # The budgets are global, not per source: every source contributes what is left of the
        # '--limit' digest records and of the 'max' full-list records.
        kept_budget=$(( HERMES_LOGS_Q_MAX - HERMES_LOGS_R_KEPT ))
        (( kept_budget < 0 )) && kept_budget=0
        show_budget=$(( HERMES_LOGS_Q_LIMIT - HERMES_LOGS_R_SHOWN ))
        (( show_budget < 0 )) && show_budget=0
        byte_budget=$(( HERMES_LOGS_Q_BYTES - HERMES_LOGS_R_BYTES ))
        (( byte_budget < 0 )) && byte_budget=0
        HERMES_LOGS_ENV=(
            "HL_PAT=$HERMES_LOGS_Q_PAT"
            "HL_ICASE=$HERMES_LOGS_Q_ICASE"
            "HL_CUTOFF=$HERMES_LOGS_Q_CUTOFF"
            "HL_SNIP=$HERMES_LOGS_Q_SNIP"
            "HL_LIMIT=$show_budget"
            "HL_BYTES=$byte_budget"
            "HL_MAX=$kept_budget"
            "HL_HITS=$HERMES_LOGS_R_HITS"
            "HL_CLIP=$HERMES_LOGS_R_CLIP"
        )
        rc=0
        if [[ "$kind" == store ]]; then
            hermes_logs_scan_store "$root/$rel" "$locator" "$mtime" || rc=$?
        else
            hermes_logs_scan_file "$root/$rel" "$locator" "$mtime" "$ses" || rc=$?
        fi
        if (( rc )); then
            HERMES_LOGS_R_UNREADABLE=$(( HERMES_LOGS_R_UNREADABLE + 1 ))
            HERMES_LOGS_R_LOST+=( "$kind/$rel" )
            printf 'hermes_logs: could not read %s, it is not part of the count\n' "$root/$rel" >&2
        fi
        if [[ -s "$HERMES_LOGS_R_STAT" ]]; then
            read -r matches snippets records drawn drawnbytes <"$HERMES_LOGS_R_STAT" || true
            HERMES_LOGS_R_TOTAL=$(( HERMES_LOGS_R_TOTAL + ${matches:-0} ))
            HERMES_LOGS_R_CLIPPED=$(( HERMES_LOGS_R_CLIPPED + ${snippets:-0} ))
            HERMES_LOGS_R_KEPT=$(( HERMES_LOGS_R_KEPT + ${records:-0} ))
            HERMES_LOGS_R_SHOWN=$(( HERMES_LOGS_R_SHOWN + ${drawn:-0} ))
            HERMES_LOGS_R_BYTES=$(( HERMES_LOGS_R_BYTES + ${drawnbytes:-0} ))
        fi
    done < <(for index in "${!HERMES_LOGS_Q_ROOTS[@]}"; do
                 hermes_logs_files "${HERMES_LOGS_Q_ROOTS[index]}" "$index" \
                     ${HERMES_LOGS_Q_KINDS[@]+"${HERMES_LOGS_Q_KINDS[@]}"}
             done)

    rc=0
    if (( HERMES_LOGS_R_UNREADABLE )); then
        rc=1
    elif (( HERMES_LOGS_R_TOTAL == 0 )); then
        rc=3
    fi
    if [[ -n "$HERMES_LOGS_Q_COUNT" ]]; then
        printf '%s\n' "$HERMES_LOGS_R_TOTAL"
    elif [[ -n "$HERMES_LOGS_Q_JSON" ]]; then
        hermes_logs_report_json
    else
        hermes_logs_report_text
    fi
    rm -f "$HERMES_LOGS_R_STAT" "$HERMES_LOGS_R_CLIP"
    return "$rc"
}

function hermes_logs
{
    ## Body of the 'hermes_logs' rule: parse the options into the query context, resolve the corpus
    ## roots and hand over to 'hermes_logs_scan'.  See the module header for the contract.
    local pat="" when="" json="" count="" arg
    local limit="$BAR_HERMES_LOGS_LIMIT"
    local -a kinds=() roots=()
    HERMES_LOGS_Q_TAG="$(hash_args "$*")"
    while (( $# )); do
        arg="$1"
        shift
        case "$arg" in
        --grep)
            if (( $# )); then pat="$1"; shift; else hermes_logs_usage; return 2; fi ;;
        -i|--ignore-case)
            HERMES_LOGS_Q_ICASE=1 ;;
        --since)
            if (( $# )); then when="$1"; shift; else hermes_logs_usage; return 2; fi ;;
        --source)
            if (( $# )); then kinds+=( "$1" ); shift; else hermes_logs_usage; return 2; fi ;;
        --task|--run)
            if (( $# )); then HERMES_LOGS_Q_TASK="$1"; shift; else hermes_logs_usage; return 2; fi ;;
        --session)
            if (( $# )); then HERMES_LOGS_Q_SESSION="$1"; shift; else hermes_logs_usage; return 2; fi ;;
        --limit)
            if (( $# )); then limit="$1"; shift; else hermes_logs_usage; return 2; fi ;;
        --root)
            if (( $# )); then roots+=( "$1" ); shift; else hermes_logs_usage; return 2; fi ;;
        --count)
            count=1 ;;
        --json)
            json=1 ;;
        *)
            printf 'hermes_logs: unknown argument: %s\n' "$arg" >&2
            hermes_logs_usage
            return 2
            ;;
        esac
    done
    HERMES_LOGS_Q_PAT="$pat"
    HERMES_LOGS_Q_LIMIT="$limit"
    if [[ -n "$json" || -n "${BAR_AGENT_JSON:-}" ]]; then
        HERMES_LOGS_Q_JSON=1
    fi
    if [[ -n "$count" ]]; then
        HERMES_LOGS_Q_COUNT=1
        HERMES_LOGS_Q_LIMIT=0
    fi
    if [[ ! "$HERMES_LOGS_Q_LIMIT" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]]; then
        printf 'hermes_logs: --limit needs a number, got %s\n' "$HERMES_LOGS_Q_LIMIT" >&2
        return 2
    fi
    HERMES_LOGS_Q_SNIP="$BAR_HERMES_LOGS_SNIPPET"
    [[ "$HERMES_LOGS_Q_SNIP" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]] || HERMES_LOGS_Q_SNIP=160
    HERMES_LOGS_Q_MAX="$BAR_HERMES_LOGS_MAX"
    [[ "$HERMES_LOGS_Q_MAX" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]] || HERMES_LOGS_Q_MAX=20000
    HERMES_LOGS_Q_BYTES="$BAR_HERMES_LOGS_BYTES"
    [[ "$HERMES_LOGS_Q_BYTES" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]] || HERMES_LOGS_Q_BYTES=1200
    local kind
    for kind in ${kinds[@]+"${kinds[@]}"}; do
        case "$kind" in
        logs|workers|cron|sessions|store)
            HERMES_LOGS_Q_KINDS+=( "$kind" ) ;;
        *)
            printf 'hermes_logs: unknown --source %s (logs workers cron sessions store)\n' "$kind" >&2
            return 2
            ;;
        esac
    done
    hermes_logs_selector --task "$HERMES_LOGS_Q_TASK" || return 2
    hermes_logs_selector --session "$HERMES_LOGS_Q_SESSION" || return 2
    if (( ${#roots[@]} )); then
        HERMES_LOGS_Q_ROOTS=( "${roots[@]}" )
    elif [[ -n "$BAR_HERMES_LOGS_ROOT" ]]; then
        local r
        while IFS= read -r r; do
            if [[ -n "$r" ]]; then HERMES_LOGS_Q_ROOTS+=( "$r" ); fi
        done < <(printf '%s\n' "$BAR_HERMES_LOGS_ROOT" | tr ':' '\n')
    else
        HERMES_LOGS_Q_ROOTS=( "${HERMES_HOME:-$HOME/.hermes}" )
    fi
    local root
    for root in "${HERMES_LOGS_Q_ROOTS[@]}"; do
        if [[ ! -d "$root" ]]; then
            printf 'hermes_logs: not a corpus root: %s\n' "$root" >&2
            return 1
        fi
    done
    if [[ -n "$when" ]]; then
        if ! hermes_logs_since "$when"; then
            printf 'hermes_logs: cannot read --since %s\n' "$when" >&2
            return 2
        fi
    fi
    hermes_logs_scan
}

# helper: hermes_logs | exact match, range and count questions over the Hermes log corpus | hermes_logs [--grep <ere>] [--since <when>] [--source <kind>].. [--task <sel>] [--session <id>] [--limit <n>] [--count] [--json] [--root <dir>].. | one line per match '<locator> <timestamp> <snippet>', then 'matches: <n>', the 'corpus:' line and, when elided, 'max: <path>'
## The one deterministic answer to 'what do the logs of this host say about <X>'.  Streams the
## corpus once (agent/gateway logs, kanban worker transcripts, cron run outputs, the session store),
## prints a bounded digest and the exact match count, and keeps the complete match list on disk.
## Exit 0 answered, 3 for no match, 2 usage error, 1 a source could not be read.  See the module
## header for the corpus, the locator format, the filters and the non goals.
rule hermes_logs: -


###
### HANDOFF BRIEFS ('hermes_handoff')
###
### A child session ('delegate_task') starts with no memory of the conversation that spawned it, so
### the caller hands it a brief.  'hermes_handoff' composes that brief, resolves its anchor phrases
### against the session store and checks that a child could retrieve the session -- one rule, three
### modes:
###
###   hermes_handoff --goal <line> [--context <text> | --context-file <path>]
###                  [--anchor <phrase>].. [--gate <line>].. [--report-chars <n>]
###                  [--session <id>] [--db <path>] [--json]
###       a brief in seven sections, in order, one heading each, plain text: GOAL, CONTEXT,
###       RETRIEVAL, ANCHORS, MECHANICS, ACCEPTANCE GATES and REPORT FORMAT.  GOAL, CONTEXT and
###       every --gate line are printed verbatim; each --anchor phrase resolves to its messages.
###   hermes_handoff --anchors <phrase>.. [--limit <n>] [--session <id>] [--db <path>] [--json]
###       one 'msg <id> <role> <snippet>' line per distinct matching message, then 'matches: <n>'.
###   hermes_handoff --verify [--session <id>] [--db <path>] [--json]
###       whether a child could retrieve this session: 'session <id> msgs=<n> chars=<n>
###       retrieval=ok|missing', then the two retrieval recipes and the live delegation caps.
###
### THE SESSION STORE
###
### The store is a read only SQLite database, '${HERMES_HOME:-$HOME/.hermes}/state.db', overridden by
### '--db <path>' or '$HANDOFF_DB'.  The session id comes from '--session <id>' or
### '$HERMES_SESSION_ID'; the profile -- the first segment of an '@session:<profile>/<id>' link --
### from '$HERMES_SESSION_PROFILE', default 'default'.  'messages' and 'sessions' are read with the
### 'sqlite3' CLI: no LLM and no summariser.  An anchor phrase resolves to the messages whose
### 'content' contains it, case insensitively; a phrase that resolves to nothing is reported as
### 'UNRESOLVED: <phrase>' and never guessed.  Nothing host local is hardcoded: the caps are read
### live with 'hermes config get delegation.<key>' and '$HERMES_MAX_ITERATIONS'.
###
### EXIT CODES
###
###   0 answered; 1 --anchors matched nothing; 2 usage error; 3 the session or the store is unknown
###   or unreadable; 4 the brief has an unresolved anchor (the whole brief is still printed).
###
### The text and the '--json' forms carry the same numbers; '--json' is one object.
###

## The one snippet expression: every control character that would break one record per line is
## replaced by a space (newline, carriage return, tab and the US field separator of this section),
## then at most 72 characters are kept.
HERMES_HANDOFF_SNIPPET_SQL="substr(replace(replace(replace(replace(coalesce(content, ''), char(10), ' '), char(13), ' '), char(9), ' '), char(31), ' '), 1, 72)"

function hermes_handoff_home ## - the Hermes home directory
{
    ## '$HERMES_HOME' when set, '~/.hermes' otherwise.  Resolved here and nowhere else so no path of
    ## one host leaks into the rule.
    printf '%s' "${HERMES_HOME:-$HOME/.hermes}"
}

function hermes_handoff_db ## <override> - the session store path
{
    ## '--db' wins, then '$HANDOFF_DB', then the store below the Hermes home.
    if [[ -n "${1:-}" ]]; then
        printf '%s' "$1"
    elif [[ -n "${HANDOFF_DB:-}" ]]; then
        printf '%s' "$HANDOFF_DB"
    else
        printf '%s/state.db' "$(hermes_handoff_home)"
    fi
}

function hermes_handoff_profile ## - the profile of an '@session:' link
{
    printf '%s' "${HERMES_SESSION_PROFILE:-default}"
}

function hermes_handoff_session ## <override> - the session id, or empty
{
    if [[ -n "${1:-}" ]]; then
        printf '%s' "$1"
    else
        printf '%s' "${HERMES_SESSION_ID:-}"
    fi
}

function hermes_handoff_trim ## <text> - <text> without leading or trailing whitespace
{
    local text="$1"
    text="${text#"${text%%[![:space:]]*}"}"
    text="${text%"${text##*[![:space:]]}"}"
    printf '%s' "$text"
}

function hermes_handoff_cap_text ## <value> - <value>, or 'unavailable' when it is empty
{
    printf '%s' "${1:-unavailable}"
}

function hermes_handoff_sql ## <db> <sql> - run one read only query, US separated fields
{
    ## 'sqlite3 -readonly' never creates a journal and never writes to the store.
    local db="$1" sql="$2"
    sqlite3 -readonly -separator $'\037' "$db" "$sql"
}

function hermes_handoff_quote ## <value> - a SQL single quoted literal
{
    local value="$1"
    printf "'%s'" "${value//\'/\'\'}"
}

function hermes_handoff_match ## <phrase> - the SQL predicate matching one anchor phrase
{
    ## A case insensitive substring match over the message content.  'instr' -- not 'like' -- is
    ## used so no wildcard of the phrase has a meaning of its own.
    printf "instr(lower(coalesce(content, '')), lower(%s)) > 0" "$(hermes_handoff_quote "$1")"
}

function hermes_handoff_store_ok ## <db> - 0 when <db> is a readable session store
{
    local db="$1" found
    [[ -f "$db" ]] || return 1
    command -v sqlite3 >/dev/null 2>&1 || return 1
    found="$(hermes_handoff_sql "$db" "select count(*) from sqlite_master where type = 'table' and name = 'messages';" 2>/dev/null)" || return 1
    [[ "$found" == 1 ]]
}

function hermes_handoff_session_exists ## <db> <session> - 0 when the session is in the store
{
    local db="$1" session="$2" found
    found="$(hermes_handoff_sql "$db" "select 1 from sessions where id = $(hermes_handoff_quote "$session") limit 1;" 2>/dev/null)" || return 1
    [[ "$found" == 1 ]]
}

function hermes_handoff_resolve ## <db> <session> <phrase> [<limit>] - the matching messages
{
    local db="$1" session="$2" phrase="$3" limit="${4:-}"
    local limit_sql=""
    [[ -n "$limit" && "$limit" != 0 ]] && limit_sql="limit $limit"
    hermes_handoff_sql "$db" "
select id, role, $HERMES_HANDOFF_SNIPPET_SQL
from messages
where session_id = $(hermes_handoff_quote "$session")
  and $(hermes_handoff_match "$phrase")
order by id
$limit_sql;"
}

function hermes_handoff_count ## <db> <session> <phrase> - the number of matching messages
{
    hermes_handoff_sql "$1" "select count(*) from messages where session_id = $(hermes_handoff_quote "$2") and $(hermes_handoff_match "$3");"
}

function hermes_handoff_stats ## <db> <session> - the message count and total content size
{
    ## Sets HERMES_HANDOFF_MSGS and HERMES_HANDOFF_CHARS.
    local row
    row="$(hermes_handoff_sql "$1" "select count(*), coalesce(sum(length(content)), 0) from messages where session_id = $(hermes_handoff_quote "$2");")"
    HERMES_HANDOFF_MSGS="$(hermes_handoff_trim "${row%%$'\037'*}")"
    HERMES_HANDOFF_CHARS="$(hermes_handoff_trim "${row#*$'\037'}")"
}

function hermes_handoff_record ## <record> - 'msg <id> <role> <snippet>' from one US record
{
    local -a f=()
    IFS=$'\037' read -r -a f <<<"$1"
    printf 'msg %s %s %s' "${f[0]:-}" "${f[1]:-}" "${f[2]:-}"
}

function hermes_handoff_config ## <key> - one 'hermes config get delegation.<key>' value, or empty
{
    command -v hermes >/dev/null 2>&1 || return 0
    hermes_handoff_trim "$(hermes config get "delegation.$1" 2>/dev/null | head -n 1)"
}

function hermes_handoff_caps ## - read the live delegation caps into the HERMES_HANDOFF_CAP_* variables
{
    ## Read live and never hardcoded: the spawn depth and the summary budget come from the Hermes
    ## configuration, the child iteration cap from '$HERMES_MAX_ITERATIONS' when set and the
    ## configuration otherwise.
    HERMES_HANDOFF_CAP_DEPTH="$(hermes_handoff_config max_spawn_depth)"
    HERMES_HANDOFF_CAP_SUMMARY="$(hermes_handoff_config max_summary_chars)"
    if [[ -n "${HERMES_MAX_ITERATIONS:-}" ]]; then
        HERMES_HANDOFF_CAP_ITERATIONS="$HERMES_MAX_ITERATIONS"
        HERMES_HANDOFF_CAP_ITERATIONS_SOURCE='$HERMES_MAX_ITERATIONS'
    else
        HERMES_HANDOFF_CAP_ITERATIONS="$(hermes_handoff_config max_iterations)"
        HERMES_HANDOFF_CAP_ITERATIONS_SOURCE='delegation.max_iterations'
    fi
}

function hermes_handoff_caps_line ## - one 'caps:' line
{
    printf 'caps: max_spawn_depth=%s max_summary_chars=%s child_iterations=%s\n' \
        "$(hermes_handoff_cap_text "$HERMES_HANDOFF_CAP_DEPTH")" \
        "$(hermes_handoff_cap_text "$HERMES_HANDOFF_CAP_SUMMARY")" \
        "$(hermes_handoff_cap_text "$HERMES_HANDOFF_CAP_ITERATIONS")"
}

function hermes_handoff_recipes ## <db> <session> - the two exact retrieval recipes
{
    printf "scroll: session_search(session_id='%s', around_message_id=<msg-id>, window=10, role_filter='user,assistant,tool')\n" "$2"
    printf '%s\n' '  the scroll shape returns the window around the anchor un-truncated; the discovery shape'
    printf '%s\n' "  (the 'query' argument) returns top-N sessions with truncated bodies, so scroll when exact text matters"
    printf "verbatim: sqlite3 -readonly '%s' \"select id, role, content from messages where session_id='%s' order by id;\"\n" "$1" "$2"
}

function hermes_handoff_json_strings ## <text..> - the texts as a JSON array of strings
{
    local out="" separator="" text literal=""
    for text in "$@"; do
        json_set_string literal "$text"
        out+="$separator$literal"
        separator=","
    done
    printf '[%s]' "$out"
}

function hermes_handoff_json_records ## <record..> - the US records as a JSON array of objects
{
    local out="" separator="" record id role snippet literal="" role_json=""
    for record in "$@"; do
        IFS=$'\037' read -r id role snippet <<<"$record"
        json_set_string literal "$role"
        role_json="$literal"
        json_set_string literal "$snippet"
        out+="$separator{\"id\":${id:-null},\"role\":$role_json,\"snippet\":$literal}"
        separator=","
    done
    printf '[%s]' "$out"
}

function hermes_handoff_usage ## - the usage text, on stderr
{
    cat >&2 <<'USAGE'
usage: bar hermes_handoff --goal <line> [--context <text> | --context-file <path>]
                          [--anchor <phrase>].. [--gate <line>].. [--report-chars <n>]
                          [--session <id>] [--db <path>] [--json]
       bar hermes_handoff --anchors <phrase>.. [--limit <n>] [--session <id>] [--db <path>] [--json]
       bar hermes_handoff --verify [--session <id>] [--db <path>] [--json]

  --goal <line>          the goal of the child, printed verbatim (a brief)
  --context <text>       context the child cannot retrieve, printed verbatim
  --context-file <path>  the context read from a file instead
  --anchor <phrase>      a phrase resolved to 'msg <id> <role> <snippet>'; repeatable
  --gate <line>          one acceptance gate, printed verbatim; repeatable
  --report-chars <n>     the report bound told to the child (default 1500)
  --anchors <phrase>..   resolve phrases and print the matches instead of a brief
  --verify               print whether a child could retrieve the session
  --limit <n>            --anchors: print at most n matches (0 = all; default 20)
  --session <id>         the session (default $HERMES_SESSION_ID)
  --db <path>            the session store (default $HANDOFF_DB or the Hermes home's state.db)
  --json                 one object with the same numbers as the text form

exit codes: 0 answered, 1 --anchors matched nothing, 2 usage error,
            3 session or store unknown/unreadable, 4 a brief anchor did not resolve
USAGE
}

function hermes_handoff_brief_text
{
    local line phrase
    printf 'GOAL\n%s\n\n' "$HERMES_HANDOFF_GOAL"
    if [[ -n "$HERMES_HANDOFF_CONTEXT" ]]; then
        printf 'CONTEXT\n%s\n\n' "$HERMES_HANDOFF_CONTEXT"
    else
        printf 'CONTEXT\n(no context given)\n\n'
    fi
    printf 'RETRIEVAL\n@session:%s/%s\n' "$(hermes_handoff_profile)" "$HERMES_HANDOFF_SESSION"
    hermes_handoff_recipes "$HERMES_HANDOFF_DB" "$HERMES_HANDOFF_SESSION"
    printf '\nANCHORS\n'
    if (( ${#HERMES_HANDOFF_PHRASES[@]} == 0 )); then
        printf '%s\n' '(no anchors given)'
    else
        for line in ${HERMES_HANDOFF_RESOLVED[@]+"${HERMES_HANDOFF_RESOLVED[@]}"}; do
            hermes_handoff_record "$line"
            printf '\n'
        done
        for phrase in ${HERMES_HANDOFF_UNRESOLVED[@]+"${HERMES_HANDOFF_UNRESOLVED[@]}"}; do
            printf 'UNRESOLVED: %s\n' "$phrase"
        done
    fi
    printf '\nMECHANICS\n'
    printf 'max_spawn_depth: %s\n' "$(hermes_handoff_cap_text "$HERMES_HANDOFF_CAP_DEPTH")"
    printf 'max_summary_chars: %s\n' "$(hermes_handoff_cap_text "$HERMES_HANDOFF_CAP_SUMMARY")"
    printf 'child_iterations: %s (from %s)\n' "$(hermes_handoff_cap_text "$HERMES_HANDOFF_CAP_ITERATIONS")" "$HERMES_HANDOFF_CAP_ITERATIONS_SOURCE"
    printf '%s\n' 'standing facts:' \
        '- a child cannot call clarify' \
        '- a child cannot write memory' \
        '- a child does not inherit the skills index; name every skill explicitly' \
        '- a command needing human approval is denied, not hung' \
        '- decide nothing - report instead'
    printf '\nACCEPTANCE GATES\n'
    if (( ${#HERMES_HANDOFF_GATES[@]} == 0 )); then
        printf '%s\n' '(no gates given)'
    else
        for line in "${HERMES_HANDOFF_GATES[@]}"; do
            printf '%s\n' "$line"
        done
    fi
    printf '\nREPORT FORMAT\n'
    printf 'report at most %s chars, and carry the handles the caller will verify:\n' "$HERMES_HANDOFF_REPORT_CHARS"
    printf '%s\n' \
        '- absolute paths of every file you created or changed' \
        '- ids: the session, message, card and run ids you touched' \
        '- shas: git HEAD and any tree you produced, and the commands you ran'
}

function hermes_handoff_brief_json
{
    local literal=""
    printf '{"bar_hermes_handoff":1,"mode":"brief","session":'
    json_set_string literal "$HERMES_HANDOFF_SESSION"
    printf '%s,"profile":' "$literal"
    json_set_string literal "$(hermes_handoff_profile)"
    printf '%s,"db":' "$literal"
    json_set_string literal "$HERMES_HANDOFF_DB"
    printf '%s,"goal":' "$literal"
    json_set_string literal "$HERMES_HANDOFF_GOAL"
    printf '%s,"context":' "$literal"
    if [[ -n "$HERMES_HANDOFF_CONTEXT" ]]; then
        json_set_string literal "$HERMES_HANDOFF_CONTEXT"
        printf '%s' "$literal"
    else
        printf 'null'
    fi
    printf ',"phrases":'
    hermes_handoff_json_strings ${HERMES_HANDOFF_PHRASES[@]+"${HERMES_HANDOFF_PHRASES[@]}"}
    printf ',"anchors":'
    hermes_handoff_json_records ${HERMES_HANDOFF_RESOLVED[@]+"${HERMES_HANDOFF_RESOLVED[@]}"}
    printf ',"anchor_count":%s' "${#HERMES_HANDOFF_RESOLVED[@]}"
    printf ',"unresolved":'
    hermes_handoff_json_strings ${HERMES_HANDOFF_UNRESOLVED[@]+"${HERMES_HANDOFF_UNRESOLVED[@]}"}
    printf ',"unresolved_count":%s' "${#HERMES_HANDOFF_UNRESOLVED[@]}"
    printf ',"mechanics":{"max_spawn_depth":%s,"max_summary_chars":%s,"child_iterations":%s,"child_iterations_source":' \
        "$(json_number "$HERMES_HANDOFF_CAP_DEPTH")" "$(json_number "$HERMES_HANDOFF_CAP_SUMMARY")" "$(json_number "$HERMES_HANDOFF_CAP_ITERATIONS")"
    json_set_string literal "$HERMES_HANDOFF_CAP_ITERATIONS_SOURCE"
    printf '%s}' "$literal"
    printf ',"gates":'
    hermes_handoff_json_strings ${HERMES_HANDOFF_GATES[@]+"${HERMES_HANDOFF_GATES[@]}"}
    printf ',"gates_count":%s' "${#HERMES_HANDOFF_GATES[@]}"
    printf ',"report_chars":%s}\n' "$HERMES_HANDOFF_REPORT_CHARS"
}

function hermes_handoff_brief_run ## <session> <db> <json> <goal> <context> <report_chars>
{
    local session="$1" db="$2" json="$3" goal="$4" context="$5" report_chars="$6"
    local phrase line total
    if [[ -z "$session" ]]; then
        printf 'hermes_handoff: no session, pass --session or set $HERMES_SESSION_ID\n' >&2
        return 3
    fi
    if ! hermes_handoff_store_ok "$db"; then
        printf 'hermes_handoff: cannot read the session store at %s\n' "$db" >&2
        return 3
    fi
    if ! hermes_handoff_session_exists "$db" "$session"; then
        printf 'hermes_handoff: no session %s in %s\n' "$session" "$db" >&2
        return 3
    fi
    HERMES_HANDOFF_SESSION="$session"
    HERMES_HANDOFF_DB="$db"
    HERMES_HANDOFF_GOAL="$goal"
    HERMES_HANDOFF_CONTEXT="$context"
    HERMES_HANDOFF_REPORT_CHARS="$report_chars"
    HERMES_HANDOFF_RESOLVED=()
    HERMES_HANDOFF_UNRESOLVED=()
    local -A seen_ids=()
    for phrase in ${HERMES_HANDOFF_PHRASES[@]+"${HERMES_HANDOFF_PHRASES[@]}"}; do
        total="$(hermes_handoff_count "$db" "$session" "$phrase")"
        if [[ "$total" == 0 ]]; then
            HERMES_HANDOFF_UNRESOLVED+=("$phrase")
            continue
        fi
        while IFS= read -r line; do
            [[ -n "$line" ]] || continue
            if [[ -z "${seen_ids["${line%%$'\037'*}"]:-}" ]]; then
                seen_ids["${line%%$'\037'*}"]=1
                HERMES_HANDOFF_RESOLVED+=("$line")
            fi
        done < <(hermes_handoff_resolve "$db" "$session" "$phrase" "")
    done
    hermes_handoff_caps
    if [[ -n "$json" ]]; then
        hermes_handoff_brief_json
    else
        hermes_handoff_brief_text
    fi
    if (( ${#HERMES_HANDOFF_UNRESOLVED[@]} > 0 )); then
        return 4
    fi
    return 0
}

function hermes_handoff_anchors_json ## <session> <db> <limit> <matched> <printed> <full>
{
    local session="$1" db="$2" limit="$3" matched="$4" printed="$5" full="$6" literal=""
    printf '{"bar_hermes_handoff":1,"mode":"anchors","session":'
    json_set_string literal "$session"
    printf '%s,"db":' "$literal"
    json_set_string literal "$db"
    printf '%s,"limit":%s,"matches":%s,"showing":%s,"full":' "$literal" "$(json_number "$limit")" "$matched" "$printed"
    if [[ -n "$full" ]]; then
        json_set_string literal "$full"
        printf '%s' "$literal"
    else
        printf 'null'
    fi
    printf ',"messages":'
    hermes_handoff_json_records ${HERMES_HANDOFF_ROWS[@]+"${HERMES_HANDOFF_ROWS[@]}"}
    printf '}\n'
}

function hermes_handoff_anchors_run ## <session> <db> <json> <limit>
{
    local session="$1" db="$2" json="$3" limit="$4"
    local -i printed=0
    local matched=0 clause="" rows="" full="" file="" tmp="" line phrase
    HERMES_HANDOFF_ROWS=()

    if [[ -z "$session" ]]; then
        printf 'hermes_handoff: no session, pass --session or set $HERMES_SESSION_ID\n' >&2
        return 3
    fi
    if ! hermes_handoff_store_ok "$db"; then
        printf 'hermes_handoff: cannot read the session store at %s\n' "$db" >&2
        return 3
    fi
    if ! hermes_handoff_session_exists "$db" "$session"; then
        printf 'hermes_handoff: no session %s in %s\n' "$session" "$db" >&2
        return 3
    fi

    for phrase in ${HERMES_HANDOFF_PHRASES[@]+"${HERMES_HANDOFF_PHRASES[@]}"}; do
        clause+="${clause:+ or }$(hermes_handoff_match "$phrase")"
    done

    matched="$(hermes_handoff_trim "$(hermes_handoff_sql "$db" "select count(*) from messages where session_id = $(hermes_handoff_quote "$session") and ($clause);")")"

    if [[ "$matched" == 0 ]]; then
        if [[ -n "$json" ]]; then
            hermes_handoff_anchors_json "$session" "$db" "$limit" 0 0 ""
        else
            printf 'matches: 0\n'
        fi
        return 1
    fi

    rows="$(hermes_handoff_sql "$db" "
select id, role, $HERMES_HANDOFF_SNIPPET_SQL
from messages
where session_id = $(hermes_handoff_quote "$session") and ($clause)
order by id
$([[ "$limit" != 0 ]] && printf 'limit %s' "$limit");")"

    if [[ -n "$rows" ]]; then
        while IFS= read -r line; do
            [[ -n "$line" ]] || continue
            printed=$(( printed + 1 ))
            HERMES_HANDOFF_ROWS+=("$line")
            if [[ -z "$json" ]]; then
                hermes_handoff_record "$line"
                printf '\n'
            fi
        done <<<"$rows"
    fi

    if (( limit != 0 && printed < matched )); then
        ## Whatever the digest leaves out stays retrievable from a file whose path is printed next
        ## to the elision counts.  Written through a temporary name.
        file="${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/hermes_handoff-${session}.txt"
        tmp="$file.$$"
        {
            while IFS= read -r line; do
                [[ -n "$line" ]] || continue
                hermes_handoff_record "$line"
                printf '\n'
            done <<<"$(hermes_handoff_sql "$db" "
select id, role, $HERMES_HANDOFF_SNIPPET_SQL
from messages
where session_id = $(hermes_handoff_quote "$session") and ($clause)
order by id;")"
        } >"$tmp"
        mv -f "$tmp" "$file"
        full="$file"
    fi

    if [[ -n "$json" ]]; then
        hermes_handoff_anchors_json "$session" "$db" "$limit" "$matched" "$printed" "$full"
    else
        if [[ -n "$full" ]]; then
            printf 'showing %s of %s (full list: %s)\n' "$printed" "$matched" "$full"
        fi
        printf 'matches: %s\n' "$matched"
    fi
    return 0
}

function hermes_handoff_verify_json ## <session> <db> <retrieval>
{
    local session="$1" db="$2" retrieval="$3" literal=""
    printf '{"bar_hermes_handoff":1,"mode":"verify","session":'
    json_set_string literal "$session"
    printf '%s,"profile":' "$literal"
    json_set_string literal "$(hermes_handoff_profile)"
    printf '%s,"db":' "$literal"
    json_set_string literal "$db"
    printf '%s,"msgs":%s,"chars":%s,"retrieval":' "$literal" "${HERMES_HANDOFF_MSGS:-0}" "${HERMES_HANDOFF_CHARS:-0}"
    json_set_string literal "$retrieval"
    printf '%s' "$literal"
    printf ',"caps":{"max_spawn_depth":%s,"max_summary_chars":%s,"child_iterations":%s,"child_iterations_source":' \
        "$(json_number "$HERMES_HANDOFF_CAP_DEPTH")" "$(json_number "$HERMES_HANDOFF_CAP_SUMMARY")" "$(json_number "$HERMES_HANDOFF_CAP_ITERATIONS")"
    json_set_string literal "$HERMES_HANDOFF_CAP_ITERATIONS_SOURCE"
    printf '%s}}\n' "$literal"
}

function hermes_handoff_verify_run ## <session> <db> <json>
{
    local session="$1" db="$2" json="$3"
    local retrieval="missing" rc=0
    if [[ -z "$session" ]]; then
        printf 'hermes_handoff: no session, pass --session or set $HERMES_SESSION_ID\n' >&2
        return 3
    fi
    HERMES_HANDOFF_SESSION="$session"
    HERMES_HANDOFF_DB="$db"
    HERMES_HANDOFF_MSGS=0
    HERMES_HANDOFF_CHARS=0
    if hermes_handoff_store_ok "$db" && hermes_handoff_session_exists "$db" "$session"; then
        hermes_handoff_stats "$db" "$session"
        [[ "$HERMES_HANDOFF_MSGS" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]] || HERMES_HANDOFF_MSGS=0
        [[ "$HERMES_HANDOFF_CHARS" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]] || HERMES_HANDOFF_CHARS=0
        if (( HERMES_HANDOFF_MSGS > 0 )); then
            retrieval="ok"
        fi
    fi
    [[ "$retrieval" == ok ]] || rc=3
    hermes_handoff_caps
    if [[ -n "$json" ]]; then
        hermes_handoff_verify_json "$session" "$db" "$retrieval"
    else
        printf 'session %s msgs=%s chars=%s retrieval=%s\n' "$session" "$HERMES_HANDOFF_MSGS" "$HERMES_HANDOFF_CHARS" "$retrieval"
        hermes_handoff_recipes "$db" "$session"
        hermes_handoff_caps_line
    fi
    return "$rc"
}

function hermes_handoff
{
    ## Body of the 'hermes_handoff' rule: parse the options, pick the mode and hand over.  See the
    ## 'HANDOFF BRIEFS' section of the module header for the modes, the store and the exit codes.
    local -a args=()
    local raw arg mode="brief" goal="" context="" context_file="" report_chars=1500 session="" db="" json="" limit="20"
    local -i count i=0

    HERMES_HANDOFF_PHRASES=()
    HERMES_HANDOFF_GATES=()
    for raw in "$@"; do
        if [[ "$raw" == --*=* ]]; then
            args+=("${raw%%=*}" "${raw#*=}")
        else
            args+=("$raw")
        fi
    done
    count=${#args[@]}
    while (( i < count )); do
        arg="${args[i]}"
        i=$(( i + 1 ))
        case "$arg" in
        --json) json=1 ;;
        --verify) mode="verify" ;;
        --anchors) mode="anchors" ;;
        --goal | --context | --context-file | --anchor | --gate | --report-chars | --session | --db | --limit)
            if (( i >= count )) || [[ -z "${args[i]}" ]]; then
                printf 'hermes_handoff: %s needs a non-empty value\n' "$arg" >&2
                hermes_handoff_usage
                return 2
            fi
            case "$arg" in
            --goal) goal="${args[i]}" ;;
            --context) context="${args[i]}" ;;
            --context-file) context_file="${args[i]}" ;;
            --anchor) HERMES_HANDOFF_PHRASES+=("${args[i]}") ;;
            --gate) HERMES_HANDOFF_GATES+=("${args[i]}") ;;
            --report-chars) report_chars="${args[i]}" ;;
            --session) session="${args[i]}" ;;
            --db) db="${args[i]}" ;;
            --limit) limit="${args[i]}" ;;
            esac
            i=$(( i + 1 ))
            ;;
        --*)
            printf 'hermes_handoff: unknown argument %s\n' "$arg" >&2
            hermes_handoff_usage
            return 2
            ;;
        *)
            HERMES_HANDOFF_PHRASES+=("$arg")
            ;;
        esac
    done

    [[ -n "${BAR_AGENT_JSON:-}" ]] && json=1

    session="$(hermes_handoff_session "$session")"
    db="$(hermes_handoff_db "$db")"

    case "$mode" in
    brief)
        if [[ -z "$goal" ]]; then
            printf 'hermes_handoff: --goal is required for a brief\n' >&2
            hermes_handoff_usage
            return 2
        fi
        if [[ ! "$report_chars" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]]; then
            printf 'hermes_handoff: invalid --report-chars %s\n' "$report_chars" >&2
            return 2
        fi
        if [[ -n "$context_file" ]]; then
            if [[ ! -r "$context_file" ]]; then
                printf 'hermes_handoff: cannot read --context-file %s\n' "$context_file" >&2
                return 2
            fi
            context="$(<"$context_file")"
        fi
        hermes_handoff_brief_run "$session" "$db" "$json" "$goal" "$context" "$report_chars"
        ;;
    anchors)
        if (( ${#HERMES_HANDOFF_PHRASES[@]} == 0 )); then
            printf 'hermes_handoff: --anchors needs at least one phrase\n' >&2
            hermes_handoff_usage
            return 2
        fi
        if [[ ! "$limit" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]]; then
            printf 'hermes_handoff: invalid --limit %s\n' "$limit" >&2
            return 2
        fi
        hermes_handoff_anchors_run "$session" "$db" "$json" "$limit"
        ;;
    verify)
        hermes_handoff_verify_run "$session" "$db" "$json"
        ;;
    esac
}

# helper: hermes_handoff | compose and verify the brief of a delegated child session | hermes_handoff [--goal <line> --context <text> or --context-file <path> --anchor <phrase>.. --gate <line>.. --report-chars <n>] [--anchors <phrase>.. --limit <n>] [--verify] [--session <id>] [--db <path>] [--json] | the brief's seven sections, or 'msg <id> <role> <snippet>' lines then 'matches: <n>', or the retrieval status line with the two recipes and the live caps
## One rule, three modes: a child session brief, the resolved anchor phrases, and whether a child
## could retrieve the session.  Reads the Hermes session store with 'sqlite3' and the delegation
## caps live -- no LLM.  Exit 0 answered, 1 --anchors matched nothing, 2 usage error, 3 the session
## or the store is unknown/unreadable, 4 the brief has an unresolved anchor.  See the module header.
rule hermes_handoff: -
